1
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,000
"The Last Oath"

2
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:04,100
(Episode 17: The Unfinished Film)

3
00:01:14,416 --> 00:01:15,416
Has he...

4
00:01:16,166 --> 00:01:17,166
always been like this?

5
00:01:20,708 --> 00:01:21,868
Ever since he was brought in.

6
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:23,500
In a way,

7
00:01:23,916 --> 00:01:26,041
this stable manic state is actually safer.

8
00:01:26,791 --> 00:01:28,416
At least I know what he'll do next.

9
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:30,720
Nothing more than ramming against the bars.

10
00:01:31,750 --> 00:01:32,750
So,

11
00:01:34,250 --> 00:01:35,916
can we start the trials today?

12
00:01:36,375 --> 00:01:37,415
What do you need me to do?

13
00:01:38,708 --> 00:01:40,068
Let's start by drawing some blood.

14
00:01:40,291 --> 00:01:41,434
We'll use it for antibody screening,

15
00:01:41,458 --> 00:01:42,416
viral inhibition experiments,

16
00:01:42,417 --> 00:01:43,916
and immune cell functional analysis.

17
00:01:48,083 --> 00:01:49,083
Come on over.

18
00:02:06,958 --> 00:02:07,958
Have a seat here.

19
00:02:17,250 --> 00:02:18,250
Roll up your sleeve.

20
00:02:18,375 --> 00:02:19,375
Rest your arm flat.

21
00:02:41,416 --> 00:02:42,416
Relax.

22
00:02:42,916 --> 00:02:43,916
Make a fist.

23
00:03:16,833 --> 00:03:17,833
Relax.

24
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,000
How much are you taking?

25
00:03:26,375 --> 00:03:27,415
Make sure you take enough.

26
00:03:28,458 --> 00:03:30,178
Let's stick to the standard amount for now.

27
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:44,375
Once you have it,

28
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:45,700
how long until we see results?

29
00:03:47,041 --> 00:03:48,041
Press down on this.

30
00:03:50,916 --> 00:03:52,083
Science isn't magic,

31
00:03:52,250 --> 00:03:52,750
Lin Zai.

32
00:03:53,125 --> 00:03:54,332
I need time to run the analysis,

33
00:03:54,333 --> 00:03:55,458
culture it, and run tests.

34
00:03:55,916 --> 00:03:56,541
Be patient.

35
00:03:56,833 --> 00:03:58,273
It's for your brother's safety, too.

36
00:03:59,416 --> 00:04:00,416
I'm patient.

37
00:04:00,875 --> 00:04:02,355
As long as it brings my brother back.

38
00:04:03,791 --> 00:04:04,583
Then let's start by

39
00:04:04,584 --> 00:04:06,165
keeping you in good health.

40
00:04:06,166 --> 00:04:07,642
We'll do another draw in a couple of days.

41
00:04:07,666 --> 00:04:09,066
I need to run a dynamic comparison.

42
00:04:16,208 --> 00:04:16,666
Come on.

43
00:04:17,166 --> 00:04:18,166
Lie down.

44
00:04:21,041 --> 00:04:22,041
Okay.

45
00:04:23,708 --> 00:04:24,625
Today, we'll just do

46
00:04:24,626 --> 00:04:26,386
some baseline checks
and sample collections.

47
00:04:26,541 --> 00:04:28,207
I have to make sure your body

48
00:04:28,208 --> 00:04:29,875
can handle future extractions.

49
00:04:30,583 --> 00:04:31,665
We can't have you collapsing

50
00:04:31,666 --> 00:04:33,026
before the cure is even developed.

51
00:04:33,583 --> 00:04:34,583
I'm healthy.

52
00:04:34,875 --> 00:04:36,515
I got bitten and didn't even run a fever.

53
00:04:37,541 --> 00:04:38,581
That's not for you to say.

54
00:04:39,166 --> 00:04:40,166
Lie still.

55
00:04:49,875 --> 00:04:50,958
The person in the video...

56
00:04:51,708 --> 00:04:52,708
what's his condition now?

57
00:04:59,833 --> 00:05:00,958
He was originally at...

58
00:05:02,583 --> 00:05:03,583
Green Island Airport.

59
00:05:04,500 --> 00:05:05,500
Green Island Airport?

60
00:05:07,208 --> 00:05:10,041
Don't tell me he's your...
brother?

61
00:05:10,833 --> 00:05:11,208
But...

62
00:05:11,209 --> 00:05:12,929
Actually, we hadn't lost contact back then.

63
00:05:13,041 --> 00:05:14,750
But given his condition,

64
00:05:15,166 --> 00:05:17,083
I couldn't tell you he was alive.

65
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:22,080
His name is Shen Changhuan.

66
00:05:22,583 --> 00:05:23,983
Our families were longtime friends.

67
00:05:24,583 --> 00:05:26,183
After my parents died in a car accident,

68
00:05:26,583 --> 00:05:28,250
his family took me in.

69
00:05:29,583 --> 00:05:30,583
Then how did he...

70
00:05:31,125 --> 00:05:32,208
how did he turn into that?

71
00:05:35,041 --> 00:05:36,041
After the outbreak,

72
00:05:37,750 --> 00:05:38,910
he was bitten by an infected.

73
00:05:39,833 --> 00:05:41,916
I used every reagent I had on him

74
00:05:42,458 --> 00:05:44,083
to slow his transformation.

75
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:47,125
But Casia found out.

76
00:05:48,791 --> 00:05:49,833
They wanted to control us,

77
00:05:51,208 --> 00:05:52,368
so I had to take him and run.

78
00:05:52,916 --> 00:05:54,556
Just as we got near Green Island Airport,

79
00:05:55,291 --> 00:05:56,625
Casia's people caught up.

80
00:05:58,625 --> 00:06:00,125
The very day we ran into you.

81
00:06:01,041 --> 00:06:02,041
Yes.

82
00:06:02,458 --> 00:06:03,583
I had to get him away,

83
00:06:04,125 --> 00:06:06,365
so I had no choice but to
trap you and steal your truck.

84
00:06:06,583 --> 00:06:07,583
But...

85
00:06:08,166 --> 00:06:09,166
I got away too late.

86
00:06:10,166 --> 00:06:11,208
When I went back for him,

87
00:06:12,500 --> 00:06:14,208
Casia had already taken him.

88
00:06:19,500 --> 00:06:20,500
So that's what happened.

89
00:06:23,166 --> 00:06:25,041
Casia has been hunting me ever since.

90
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:28,583
I'm sorry for
keeping it from you.

91
00:06:35,250 --> 00:06:36,250
I understand.

92
00:06:38,583 --> 00:06:39,583
So,

93
00:06:39,666 --> 00:06:40,986
this isn't just about my brother.

94
00:06:45,291 --> 00:06:46,416
For both of us,

95
00:06:47,291 --> 00:06:48,291
this is an experiment

96
00:06:49,833 --> 00:06:50,958
we cannot afford to lose.

97
00:07:37,208 --> 00:07:39,328
Where were you? I've been
looking everywhere for you.

98
00:07:42,583 --> 00:07:43,583
Nowhere.

99
00:07:43,833 --> 00:07:44,833
Just taking a walk.

100
00:07:47,416 --> 00:07:47,958
Lin Zai,

101
00:07:48,291 --> 00:07:50,211
if something's going on,
you have to talk to me.

102
00:07:54,416 --> 00:07:55,416
A-Leh,

103
00:07:55,833 --> 00:07:57,916
don't you think you're overstepping lately?

104
00:08:01,666 --> 00:08:02,666
Lin Zai...

105
00:08:02,791 --> 00:08:03,791
What is wrong with you?

106
00:08:04,125 --> 00:08:05,375
We were fine before.

107
00:08:13,666 --> 00:08:14,666
Can you just act normal?

108
00:08:15,250 --> 00:08:16,250
I hate this.

109
00:08:17,583 --> 00:08:18,663
Stop tailing me everywhere.

110
00:08:19,041 --> 00:08:20,083
Give me some space.

111
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:16,500
Changhuan.

112
00:09:17,541 --> 00:09:18,541
Changhuan.

113
00:09:25,916 --> 00:09:26,916
Brother...

114
00:09:34,458 --> 00:09:34,916
How is it?

115
00:09:35,375 --> 00:09:36,375
How are you feeling?

116
00:09:41,208 --> 00:09:41,875
What are these...?

117
00:09:41,876 --> 00:09:43,291
New equipment I managed to set up.

118
00:09:47,791 --> 00:09:48,791
How do you feel?

119
00:09:56,541 --> 00:09:57,750
This isn't your blood.

120
00:09:59,875 --> 00:10:00,875
You could tell?

121
00:10:01,333 --> 00:10:02,333
Does it feel different?

122
00:10:03,958 --> 00:10:04,958
Very different.

123
00:10:05,625 --> 00:10:07,540
That noise in my head...

124
00:10:07,541 --> 00:10:08,708
it's completely gone.

125
00:10:09,833 --> 00:10:10,833
And...

126
00:10:10,958 --> 00:10:12,166
ever since I became like this,

127
00:10:12,916 --> 00:10:14,500
my head has never felt clearer.

128
00:10:15,708 --> 00:10:16,708
It really is working.

129
00:10:16,833 --> 00:10:17,250
Changhuan,

130
00:10:17,750 --> 00:10:19,083
I found an immune subject.

131
00:10:21,125 --> 00:10:22,125
An immune?

132
00:10:22,458 --> 00:10:23,500
Do they really exist?

133
00:10:25,125 --> 00:10:25,458
Changhuan,

134
00:10:26,041 --> 00:10:27,166
I told you I'd cure you.

135
00:10:28,083 --> 00:10:29,666
The data doesn't lie.

136
00:10:31,375 --> 00:10:32,375
Your neural reflexes,

137
00:10:32,541 --> 00:10:33,125
your cognitive function...

138
00:10:33,291 --> 00:10:35,211
the recovery is far more
noticeable than before.

139
00:10:35,625 --> 00:10:36,665
It's not fully stable yet,

140
00:10:37,416 --> 00:10:38,576
but we're on the right track.

141
00:10:39,083 --> 00:10:40,375
We found the key, Changhuan.

142
00:10:43,833 --> 00:10:44,833
But...

143
00:10:46,208 --> 00:10:47,208
an immune subject...

144
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:49,000
what about that person?

145
00:10:49,875 --> 00:10:51,208
Is he okay?

146
00:10:53,083 --> 00:10:54,083
Don't worry.

147
00:10:54,333 --> 00:10:55,333
He volunteered.

148
00:10:55,875 --> 00:10:57,155
He knows what he's getting into.

149
00:10:57,791 --> 00:10:59,191
He has someone he has to save, too.

150
00:10:59,541 --> 00:11:00,541
We're partners in this.

151
00:11:02,250 --> 00:11:02,500
Then...

152
00:11:03,166 --> 00:11:04,208
he won't be harmed?

153
00:11:05,291 --> 00:11:07,691
I'll strictly monitor the volume
and frequency of the draws.

154
00:11:07,750 --> 00:11:09,166
I'll minimize the toll on his body

155
00:11:09,583 --> 00:11:10,750
and ensure his safety.

156
00:11:11,458 --> 00:11:12,458
This is our only hope,

157
00:11:14,166 --> 00:11:15,416
and it's his, too.

158
00:11:20,250 --> 00:11:21,250
Come on.

159
00:11:21,666 --> 00:11:22,291
Try walking around.

160
00:11:22,458 --> 00:11:23,458
Okay.

161
00:11:26,166 --> 00:11:26,666
Take it slow.

162
00:11:27,125 --> 00:11:28,125
No rush.

163
00:11:30,166 --> 00:11:31,166
How does it feel?

164
00:11:31,333 --> 00:11:32,375
Any pain or discomfort?

165
00:11:34,208 --> 00:11:35,208
I feel good.

166
00:11:45,666 --> 00:11:46,666
By the way, Brother,

167
00:11:47,541 --> 00:11:48,750
is the antibody titer stable?

168
00:11:49,291 --> 00:11:50,707
The exact neutralization mechanism...

169
00:11:50,708 --> 00:11:52,041
any new findings on that?

170
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:54,000
If the effect holds,

171
00:11:54,708 --> 00:11:56,041
does that mean

172
00:11:56,375 --> 00:11:57,375
our previous hypothesis

173
00:11:57,416 --> 00:11:58,976
on prefusion conformation stabilization

174
00:11:59,416 --> 00:12:00,375
was the right path

175
00:12:00,376 --> 00:12:01,456
for in vivo neutralization?

176
00:12:05,125 --> 00:12:05,583
Take a look.

177
00:12:06,083 --> 00:12:07,363
The titer is exceptionally high.

178
00:12:07,458 --> 00:12:08,624
What's more, it seems to stimulate

179
00:12:08,625 --> 00:12:10,624
signs of self-repair in
damaged neural cells.

180
00:12:10,625 --> 00:12:11,707
It's not just neutralization.

181
00:12:11,708 --> 00:12:13,748
The mechanism is far more
complex than we imagined,

182
00:12:13,791 --> 00:12:14,958
involving immunomodulation.

183
00:12:15,291 --> 00:12:15,833
Right.

184
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:18,240
Stabilizing the prefusion
conformation might be the key.

185
00:12:18,500 --> 00:12:19,540
The subject's antibodies

186
00:12:19,541 --> 00:12:20,915
seem to target conserved epitopes

187
00:12:20,916 --> 00:12:21,958
we previously overlooked.

188
00:12:22,208 --> 00:12:23,208
And this...

189
00:12:23,666 --> 00:12:24,666
and this.

190
00:12:24,708 --> 00:12:25,875
Look at these parameters.

191
00:12:26,416 --> 00:12:27,496
They're entirely different.

192
00:12:27,750 --> 00:12:28,750
Incredible.

193
00:12:29,208 --> 00:12:31,000
Totally different from what we had before.

194
00:12:32,125 --> 00:12:33,625
We really did find the key.

195
00:12:47,166 --> 00:12:48,250
Your lucid periods

196
00:12:48,541 --> 00:12:50,291
are lasting far longer than ever before.

197
00:12:52,625 --> 00:12:53,916
Rest easy, Changhuan.

198
00:12:54,375 --> 00:12:55,375
This time,

199
00:12:55,750 --> 00:12:57,208
we're going home together.

200
00:12:57,958 --> 00:12:58,958
I promise.

201
00:13:40,041 --> 00:13:42,666
How's it going on your end?

202
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:45,416
Don't worry. Better than expected.

203
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,000
We can keep going.

204
00:13:47,708 --> 00:13:48,708
How are you feeling?

205
00:13:49,041 --> 00:13:49,958
I'm fine.

206
00:13:49,958 --> 00:13:50,958
Don't worry about me.

207
00:13:52,583 --> 00:13:53,875
I found some wild fruit.

208
00:13:54,208 --> 00:13:55,208
A bit sour,

209
00:13:55,416 --> 00:13:56,916
but good for some vitamins.

210
00:13:59,958 --> 00:14:01,083
I'll bring some over later.

211
00:14:02,833 --> 00:14:03,375
I should go.

212
00:14:03,583 --> 00:14:04,583
Okay.

213
00:14:21,291 --> 00:14:22,291
Can I help you?

214
00:14:26,458 --> 00:14:27,665
Getting cozy with him...

215
00:14:27,666 --> 00:14:28,791
what's your real angle?

216
00:14:31,916 --> 00:14:32,916
Pal,

217
00:14:33,416 --> 00:14:34,500
what are you getting at?

218
00:14:35,125 --> 00:14:36,790
Lin Zai and I are just
helping each other out,

219
00:14:36,791 --> 00:14:37,875
having a chat.

220
00:14:38,291 --> 00:14:39,375
In a place like this,

221
00:14:39,875 --> 00:14:41,583
there aren't many people you can talk to.

222
00:14:42,541 --> 00:14:44,500
Helping out? Chatting?

223
00:14:46,041 --> 00:14:47,250
He looks terrible.

224
00:14:48,041 --> 00:14:49,500
What were you two whispering about?

225
00:14:52,083 --> 00:14:54,040
Lin Zai's been looking worn out lately.

226
00:14:54,041 --> 00:14:55,540
I was just checking on a friend,

227
00:14:55,541 --> 00:14:56,790
and sharing

228
00:14:56,791 --> 00:14:57,708
some food I found.

229
00:14:57,709 --> 00:14:58,833
Is that a crime?

230
00:15:01,208 --> 00:15:02,208
On the other hand,

231
00:15:02,666 --> 00:15:04,040
Lin Zai doesn't seem too eager

232
00:15:04,041 --> 00:15:05,041
to talk to you.

233
00:15:06,083 --> 00:15:08,250
Aren't you being a bit too controlling?

234
00:15:08,416 --> 00:15:09,708
Giving him some breathing room

235
00:15:09,833 --> 00:15:11,000
wouldn't kill you, would it?

236
00:15:17,250 --> 00:15:18,333
Stay away from him.

237
00:15:20,041 --> 00:15:22,125
Don't let me catch you
hanging around him again.

238
00:15:22,875 --> 00:15:23,875
Or else.

239
00:16:39,541 --> 00:16:40,625
So you are awake.

240
00:16:54,583 --> 00:16:55,583
A-Leh.

241
00:16:56,291 --> 00:16:57,333
Does everything I say

242
00:16:57,666 --> 00:16:59,416
just go in one ear and out the other?

243
00:17:05,041 --> 00:17:06,321
I gave you the space you wanted.

244
00:17:06,833 --> 00:17:07,833
And what happened?

245
00:17:09,958 --> 00:17:10,958
I take a step back,

246
00:17:11,291 --> 00:17:13,011
and you take a step closer to someone else.

247
00:17:13,375 --> 00:17:14,499
Who even is He Yao?

248
00:17:14,500 --> 00:17:15,860
How well do you actually know him?

249
00:17:16,125 --> 00:17:17,415
He sidles up to you out of nowhere,

250
00:17:17,416 --> 00:17:19,216
shows a little kindness,
and you just buy it?

251
00:17:20,666 --> 00:17:21,666
Lin Zai,

252
00:17:22,416 --> 00:17:23,416
he's dangerous.

253
00:17:23,708 --> 00:17:24,708
You have no idea

254
00:17:24,709 --> 00:17:26,041
what he wants from you.

255
00:17:26,333 --> 00:17:27,416
- His background—
- Enough!

256
00:17:29,708 --> 00:17:31,375
Stop deflecting onto other people.

257
00:17:37,666 --> 00:17:39,375
You want an answer, don't you?

258
00:17:40,541 --> 00:17:41,541
Fine.

259
00:17:42,625 --> 00:17:43,875
I'll tell you right now.

260
00:17:48,666 --> 00:17:49,666
Between us,

261
00:17:50,250 --> 00:17:51,330
it's never going to happen.

262
00:17:53,083 --> 00:17:54,363
Everything that happened before,

263
00:17:55,541 --> 00:17:56,541
pretend it never existed.

264
00:17:57,583 --> 00:17:58,583
It ends here.

265
00:18:01,041 --> 00:18:02,041
Why?

266
00:18:02,333 --> 00:18:03,333
Why?!

267
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:07,375
Because you're a mercenary,

268
00:18:07,833 --> 00:18:09,291
and I'm just an ordinary person.

269
00:18:16,291 --> 00:18:17,651
We don't belong in the same world.

270
00:18:19,541 --> 00:18:20,541
A-Leh.

271
00:18:21,208 --> 00:18:22,208
You've just...

272
00:18:24,125 --> 00:18:25,565
you've just been alone for too long.

273
00:18:26,875 --> 00:18:27,955
You're mistaking an impulse

274
00:18:28,333 --> 00:18:29,333
for love.

275
00:18:39,375 --> 00:18:40,250
I'm not an idiot.

276
00:18:40,251 --> 00:18:41,541
I know what I feel.

277
00:18:44,041 --> 00:18:45,375
When you smile, I'm happy.

278
00:18:46,041 --> 00:18:46,833
When you're hurting,

279
00:18:46,833 --> 00:18:47,583
it tears me apart inside.

280
00:18:47,583 --> 00:18:48,541
When you get close to someone else,

281
00:18:48,542 --> 00:18:49,666
it makes my skin crawl.

282
00:18:54,625 --> 00:18:55,745
The first time I kissed you,

283
00:19:01,875 --> 00:19:03,541
I didn't know why I did it either.

284
00:19:05,041 --> 00:19:06,041
But...

285
00:19:06,291 --> 00:19:07,291
afterward,

286
00:19:08,916 --> 00:19:10,356
it took me back to when I was a kid,

287
00:19:12,625 --> 00:19:14,250
the very first time I ever ate my fill.

288
00:19:23,500 --> 00:19:24,500
Lin Zai.

289
